        "title": "Dynamical Systems - The Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A dynamical system is a rule for evolving a **state** forward in time. That is all. The state\nlives in a space (the **phase space**); the rule is either a vector field (continuous time) or a\nmap (discrete time). Everything in this directory — fixed points, limit cycles, bifurcations,\nchaos, strange attractors — is the study of the *long-term geometry* of trajectories under that\nrule, **without** demanding a closed-form solution."
    },
